From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:15:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(input): retain native Bedrock mining gestures

Keep an active same-position Bedrock Survival target when the held tool changes. Java includes held-item equality in sameDestroyTarget and otherwise resets progress with Abort/Start. Preserve the item check in other modes, including unmeasured Adventure restrictions, and retain the original predicate for Java sessions. An inactive target still needs a fresh Start, including a server-restored block after a miss.

Use the native accumulated-progress cutoff 0.99999F for Bedrock connections. Original Windows 1.26.60.5/protocol 2225 instructions compare against float bits 0x3f7fff58 at 0x14376af17 (REA ev_6f30800ebf6176548674907e82a3043052499a8d53cd115be3045250fd6f691b). Native and installed hand/stone controls complete after 150 positive contributions even though the last float sum is below 1. Modify only Java 26.3 continueDestroyBlock's fourth float-1 literal; its tutorial, tick and instant-start checks remain unchanged.

For negotiated Survival mining, retain held attack across completed blocks and wait on a monotonic deadline before retargeting. Native initializes the inter-block interval to 250 ms (constructor REA ev_2239fa69209f8e044a7d5402038b28b53e27ea7bf955c472b25368d84f862c88). Original-instruction controls and bounded live observation ev_b94b026ed1f8594aba3eb27938386f18ee34bd01983203bff8d3795e69ddfc9f verify the live interval, wait policy and target preservation. If the current per-update rate already reaches the native cutoff, its completion branch adds no wait. Capture the actual contribution rate to preserve that distinction.

A changed target initializes zero progress after the deadline, so do not credit the automatic fresh-click contribution on that retarget. Fresh clicks and automatic starts after an inactive target retain their first damage update. Report held-target admission before Minecraft.continueAttack, and report cancellation before a fresh start or stopDestroyBlock even if Java already cleared isDestroying. A release, miss or fresh press clears the retained local deadline. The core maps retained retargets to Continue and owns Abort/Start frame ordering.

Negotiate the versioned core mining-input extension before using this lifecycle. Old cores keep the existing two-frame closing pause, advanced by game-mode ticks so misses cannot carry it into a fresh press. Keep the separate creative delay and Java sessions on their original paths. Fold these changes into the owning mining feature rather than stacking a repair patch.

Matched controls supply fresh vanilla tools, fixed stone targets and Survival/easy with full health and hunger. Installed selectors, the three-block gesture, current-tool requests, durability and cancel/repress behavior require a running client; helper-only unit tests do not apply mixins. Complete REA records retain artifact hashes and supplied execution limits. Debugger observations establish values and order, not uninstrumented latency. The selected uninstrumented chain comparison still admits retargeting in a later input, so callback-phase parity remains open. The rapid completed-break repress lead is traced to Java attack missTime: a fresh press on temporary air sets ten ticks, then blocks held mining after the server restores the target. Read-only main-thread observation REA ev_d852d56e62a2311ee1d4bd84a8b2d2c01bfc039d6dd3b5dbbdf71b7ee25d4985 binds the restored stone and BLOCK raycast to eight countdown ticks while the mining deadline is zero. Ignore missTime only in continueAttack for the negotiated Bedrock Survival path, and use the same admission when reporting held mining. The startAttack timer and entity attack admission remain unchanged. Native control resumes a fresh five-input attempt after restoration. The installed correction resumes at input 9 instead of baseline 18; native resumes at 10. Both admitted attempts take five inputs. REA ev_aeb4b652c7eca4e3705d6b2a16e7a7ee211e926b2cea6e4154dfe8efb4e2e959 verifies the installed four-case control. Request semantics and final durability match native; each session-local stack ID is independently joined to its own authoritative inventory updates. Exact one-input phase differences remain open. Broader tool/effect and creative timing remain unmeasured.

